      },
      "message": "fix: re-export public API names (Agent, Body, FileSystemTransport, et al.) so the package's own test suite imports\n\ntests/test_agent.py, test_edge_cases.py, test_heartbeat.py, test_packet.py and\ntest_transport.py all bind these names at the cns_bridge top level, but\n__init__.py only re-exported the packet/protocol/substrate subset. Result: 5 of\n16 test modules failed at collection (ImportError) on a fresh clone.\n\nFix is purely additive: pull in the existing classes from agent/heartbeat/\npacket/protocol/transport and add an __all__. No behavior change to any\nalready-importable name.\n\nReceipts (Python 3.12.14, repo's pytest config):\n- before: python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -> exit 2, '5 errors during collection'\n- after:  python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -> exit 0, 395 passed in 5.04s\n- README command still OK: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m unittest tests.test_substrate -> 6/6 OK",
      "tree": {
